"65_winui_host_tests.mst — WinUiHostWg5bTests, the headless half of WG5b-2's
 acceptance (docs/ROADMAP.md's WG5 row, its Accept clause).

 THE SPLIT IS DIFFERENT HERE, and the difference is the interesting part.

 Every earlier winui test file is window-free because Win32 is not available
 in a CLI run. This one is window-free too — but it is NOT host-free. The FFI
 `library:` channel WG5b-2 added resolves `winui_host.dll` through
 LoadLibraryA, and the suite runs from the same directory the DLL is built
 into, so these tests exercise the REAL channel: a real DLL, a real
 `image_store` linked into it, real UTF-16 marshalling both ways.

 That is deliberate. The channel is this slice's genuinely novel machinery
 and the one most likely to be wrong, and a test that mocked it would prove
 nothing about it. What stays out is only what needs a WINDOW — a click on
 the Accept cell, the pane repainting — which is `just gate-wg5b`.

 WHAT IS NOT TESTED HERE, and why: the WRITE path. `MacvmHostSaveMethod`
 writes whatever `MACVM_IMAGE_PATH` names, defaulting to
 `world/image.sqlite3` — the repo's own image. A test suite that wrote there
 would mutate the tree it is testing, and one that silently did so would be a
 genuinely nasty thing to leave behind. Writes belong to `just gate-wg5b`,
 which points MACVM_IMAGE_PATH at a scratch copy first and is also where the
 CG8 byte-identity comparison lives.

 LOADING: as 64 — the layer files load from tests.list ahead of this one."

TestCase subclass: WinUiHostWg5bTests [

    runAll [
        "The channel first: if it is not there, every later assertion is
         about a fallback rather than about the host service, and saying so
         plainly beats fourteen confusing failures."
        self runTest: #testTheChannelResolves do: [ self testTheChannelResolves ].
        self runTest: #testAvailabilityIsRemembered do: [ self testAvailabilityIsRemembered ].

        "Then marshalling, which is where a host service actually breaks."
        self runTest: #testAReadRoundTripsItsMessage do: [ self testAReadRoundTripsItsMessage ].
        self runTest: #testAMissingClassIsRefusedNotCrashed
             do: [ self testAMissingClassIsRefusedNotCrashed ].

        "Then the pure decisions the source pane makes, which need no host."
        self runTest: #testNoClassSelectedAsksForOne do: [ self testNoClassSelectedAsksForOne ].
        self runTest: #testAClassWithNoSelectorShowsItsVariables
             do: [ self testAClassWithNoSelectorShowsItsVariables ].
        self runTest: #testTheSideDefaultsToInstance do: [ self testTheSideDefaultsToInstance ].
        self runTest: #testAcceptWithNothingSelectedRefusesQuietly
             do: [ self testAcceptWithNothingSelectedRefusesQuietly ]
    ]

    "── The channel ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────"

    testTheChannelResolves [
        "WG5b-2's one core change, proved end to end: an FFI pragma naming
         `library: #'winui_host.dll'` reaches a DLL that is in neither winkb
         nor the five-DLL probe list. Before this, nothing in Smalltalk could
         call Rust that lived downstream of the VM at all.

         The sentinel exists for exactly this assertion: a resolution failure
         and a `flows` refusal are otherwise indistinguishable from the guest
         (`the primitive failed`, both), and they are entirely different
         problems."
        self assert: WinHost available
            description: 'winui_host.dll must resolve — build it with `cargo build -p winui_host`, which drops it beside the executable where LoadLibraryA looks'.
        self assert: WinHost ping = 16r5747
            description: 'the ping sentinel identifies the DLL as OURS, not a same-named export that happened to resolve'
    ]

    testAvailabilityIsRemembered [
        "Cached, because a miss costs a LoadLibraryA per call and the answer
         cannot change within a run."
        | first |
        first := WinHost available.
        self assert: WinHost available = first
            description: 'availability must be stable across calls'
    ]

    "── Marshalling ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────"

    testAReadRoundTripsItsMessage [
        "UTF-16 out and UTF-16 back, by COUNT rather than by scanning for a
         terminator — the host reports a length excluding the NUL for exactly
         this reason, and one extra unit would put a stray NUL on the end of
         every line the transcript shows.

         THE IMAGE MAY NOT EXIST, and that is not a failure to assert against.
         `world/image.sqlite3` is a GENERATED artifact — a fresh checkout has
         none until `import_world` builds one — so this suite must pass in
         both states or it is really a test of whether someone remembered to
         run the importer.

         What is asserted either way is what this test is actually about: the
         call ANSWERS. A `#(ok message)` pair comes back with a real String in
         it whether the image was there or not, which is the whole claim being
         made about the channel — text crosses it faithfully and absence is
         reported rather than faulted. `just gate-wg5b` is where a read is
         checked against a real image with real content."
        | r |
        WinHost available ifFalse: [ ^self ].
        r := WinHost methodSourceFor: 'Object' side: #instance selector: 'printString'.
        self assert: (r at: 2) isString
            description: 'the message must come back as a String, image or no image'.
        (r at: 1)
            ifTrue: [
                self assert: (r at: 2) notNil
                    description: 'a successful read answers the stored source, possibly empty' ]
            ifFalse: [
                self assert: (r at: 2) isEmpty not
                    description: 'a failed read must carry a reason — an empty error is a dead end for whoever hits it' ]
    ]

    testAMissingClassIsRefusedNotCrashed [
        "The failure mode that matters: a name with no class behind it must
         come back as an ordinary answer, not a fault. `flows` and
         `image_store` both treat absence as data, and the marshalling layer
         must not turn that into an access violation on the way past."
        | r |
        WinHost available ifFalse: [ ^self ].
        r := WinHost methodSourceFor: 'NoSuchClassExistsHere' side: #instance selector: 'nope'.
        self assert: (r at: 2) isString
            description: 'a miss must still answer a String, so the pane always has something to show'
    ]

    "── The source pane's decisions, which are pure ──────────────────────"

    testNoClassSelectedAsksForOne [
        self assert: (WinShell sourceTextFor: nil selector: nil) = 'Select a class.'
            description: 'an empty browser must ask for a class rather than show an empty box, which reads as a failed load'
    ]

    testAClassWithNoSelectorShowsItsVariables [
        "A class with no selector chosen shows the class, not a blank — and it
         says what to do next, which is the affordance an empty source pane
         otherwise lacks entirely."
        | t |
        t := WinShell sourceTextFor: 'Point' selector: nil.
        self assert: (t startsWith: 'Point')
            description: 'the class name leads'.
        self assert: (t includesSubstring: 'Accept')
            description: 'and it names the verb that would write what the user types'
    ]

    testTheSideDefaultsToInstance [
        "Instance is the overwhelmingly common case, and a wrong guess writes
         to the wrong side of the class — which is a bug the user discovers
         only when the method they wrote cannot be found."
        WinShell selectBrowserSide: nil.
        self assert: WinShell browserSelectedSide == #instance
            description: 'the default side must be #instance'.
        WinShell selectBrowserSide: #class.
        self assert: WinShell browserSelectedSide == #class
            description: 'and an explicit choice must win'.
        WinShell selectBrowserSide: #instance
    ]

    testAcceptWithNothingSelectedRefusesQuietly [
        "Accept with no class selected must decline and SAY so, rather than
         writing to whatever was last selected — which is the shape of an
         accident that silently edits the wrong class."
        | before |
        WinShell selectBrowserClass: nil.
        before := WinShell acceptCount.
        WinShell acceptSource.
        self assert: WinShell acceptCount = before
            description: 'nothing may be written when nothing is selected'
    ]
]
